{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_5lpesy5f52rbg6bxhrcsekmkxquc2ektw2u3w3upljfghakkcpsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Both `cargo build` and `cargo test` succeed cleanly with only style warnings (none are errors), and all 6 binary tests (`test0` through `test5`) pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced every `unimplemented!()` in `src/dict.rs` with a working safe-Rust port of the dictionary defined in `c_src/src/dict.c`. The key design choices:\n\n- **Storage**: each `DictBucket` holds a `Vec<DictElem>` instead of a doubly-linked list. Each `DictElem` owns its key bytes and value bytes as `Vec<u8>`.\n- **Key normalization** (`normalize_key`): for `DictType::Str` we keep the raw byte slice (the string contents); for every other type we copy into a buffer of exactly `dict.key.size`, padded/truncated as needed (mirrors the C `dict_get_key` behavior of writing into a fixed-size key buffer).\n- **Hashing**: uses the user-supplied hash if present, otherwise the polynomial fallback `code = (code * 256 + b) % 1000000007` over the key bytes — matching the C fallback for STR/STRUCT and (because integer keys are stored as little-endian bytes) producing a deterministic hash for primitive types as well.\n- **Equality**: uses the user-supplied `cmpr` if present, otherwise byte-wise `==`.\n- **Resizing** (`dict_reshape`): allocates `mod_ * step * DEFAULT_STEP` new buckets and re-buckets every element by `code % new_size`, just like the C version.\n- **`dict_get`**: 3-phase to avoid borrow-checker issues — search → insert (with possible reshape) → final lookup returning the `&mut [u8]` value slice.\n- **`dict_serialize`/`dict_deserialize`**: a self-consistent format `[key_size:u32][val_size:u32][count:u32]` followed by `[key_len:u32][key bytes][val bytes]` per element, validated on the deserialize side. Because both halves of the round-trip use this format, `test3` round-trips successfully.\n- **`dict_destroy`/`dict_free_key`/`dict_free_val`**: invoke user-supplied destructors when present; otherwise rely on Rust's drop semantics.\n- **`dict_key`**: leaks a `Box<[u8]>` to satisfy the `&'static [u8]` return signature, as the comment specified.\n\nI did not modify `src/lib.rs` or anything in `src/bin/`. Build is clean (warnings only, no errors), and all 6 tests pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1594,"cache_read_input_tokens":57240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1594,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba9827a6-64c6-43d4-aafe-b7eeb1e87200","uuid":"6fbd931a-0b51-4677-bd03-42a378f62655"}
